# Submitting the review

- Record each finding with `add_finding`.
  Findings must anchor to lines inside the PR diff.
- On a re-review, reconcile open findings: when code fixed one, call `update_finding(id, status="resolved", note=...)`; when a human reply proves one invalid, call `resolve_finding_thread(finding_id, status="dismissed", note=...)`.
  Notes are posted verbatim as the GitHub reply.
- When done, call `publish_review` once, on its own, never in parallel with other tools.
  Pass every new open finding ID in `ranking`, most important first.
  If it returns `expected_finding_ids`, rank exactly those and call again.
  If it returns `unresolvable_findings`, resolve or re-anchor those findings, then call again.
- Report the outcome from the `publish_review` result.
  Only a numeric `review_id` with neither `dry_run` nor `skipped_empty_re_review` set means a review was posted.

This review is read-only: do not commit, push, or submit reviews or approvals through `gh` or any other path.
